--
[Verse 1]
.Em
 I’m not a black belt, but I kicked my desk
.Am
 Slack blew up while I tried to rest
.Em
 I’m not a coder, but I write like hell
.B7
 StackOverflow taught me well

.Em
 Jira says Its “in review”
.Am
 But It's been stalling since 92
.Em
 Not a musician, but I drop these tracks
.B7
 On a Amiga with a beat that slaps

[Chorus]
.Em
 Next level, say it loud
.Am
 Still can’t exit Vim, but I’m feelin' proud
.Em
 My test suite built on dreams
.B7
 And my code's run therapy memes

.Em
 Next level, I show up late
.Am
 Forgot my gi, but I still rotate
.Em
 Not the pro you think I am—
.B7
 But I’ll crush a Kanban plan

[Verse 2]
.Em
 JIRA alerts 3 AM last night
.Am
 Confluence doc said “this ain't right”
.Em
 My Git history is my shame
.B7
 “final-FINAL-v2” is my middle name
--
--
.Em
 Not a drummer, but I quantize pain
.Am
 Punch the keys till they scream my name
.Em
 Not a dev, but I git the gist
.B7
 My pull request came with a plot twist

[Chorus]
.Em
 Next level, feeling wild
.Am
 Still confuse = sign with double == sign
.Em
 I may not know what I’m doing, true—
.B7
 But neither does your senior dev crew
 
.Em
 Next level, wingin' it all
.Am
 Writing bash like it's improv call
.Em
 Cursor calls me the one
.B7
 Every crash log’s a part of the fun
 
 [Final Chorus – Loud, unqualified, unstoppable]
.Em
 Next level, built on hope
.Am
 And duct-taped scripts that barely cope
.Em
 Not a guru, sensei, or bro
.B7
 But I’m slamming keys and stealing the show
 
.Em
 Next level, imposter pride
.Am
 A warrior with Git on the side
.Em
 You can doubt me—but I won’t quit
.B7
 'Cause next level it don't retreat
